course: dictionary
lesson: 103
title: A penguin named after a place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words start with a capital letter because they are names. Adélie is a name for a kind of penguin, and it also comes from the name of a place. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: «Adelie and gentoo penguins build nests of pebbles that keep eggs out of meltwater and mud.» Penguins build nests, so Adelie must mean a kind of penguin. Ask: what word would fit here? A kind of animal fits, and the rest of the sentence tells you which animal.
explain: Adélie Land is a part of the Antarctic coast. The penguin takes its name from that land, and the land is named after Adèle, the wife of the French explorer who found it. A name can travel from a person to a place and then to an animal.
fact: An Adélie is a kind of penguin that lives in Antarctica.
fact: Adélie penguins are black and white, with a white ring round each eye.
fact: Adélie penguins are one of the most common penguins.
fact: Adélie Land is part of the Antarctic coast, named after Adèle, the wife of a French explorer.
exercise: «Adelie penguins build nests of stones.» What is an Adelie? | *A kind of penguin | A stone used for building | A kind of ice | A French explorer
exercise: Adélie Land is named after whom? | A French king | A penguin | A scientist who studies ice | *Adèle, the wife of a French explorer
exercise: What colour is the ring round each Adélie's eye? | Yellow | Black | Red | *White
test: The penguin is called Adélie because of a place. Which place? | *Adélie Land | The Antarctic coast in general | France | Antarctica
test: «Adelie penguins steal nest stones from each other, because good stones are hard to find.» Why do they steal? | *Good stones are hard to find | They like the colour of stones | They want to be famous | Stones keep them warm in summer
exam: Which best describes Adélie Land? | A French explorer who found penguins | A kind of stone used for nests | A penguin that lives in France | *A part of the Antarctic coast named after Adèle
